// Stability criteria â€” dated, pre-registered (METHODOLOGY R6, engine.md).
//
// GENERATION 3, registered 2026-07-31. Supersedes the 2026-07-20 v1 file, which
// remains in git history so every certificate scored under it stays reproducible.
//
// WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY. v1's SWINGING used `Damping(max_ratio: 0.72)` â€”
// std(second half)/std(first half) of the raw *level*. Standard deviation is
// homogeneous of degree one, so that statistic falls whenever the level falls,
// whatever the series is actually doing. Measured on synthetic series with a
// known answer: a monotone geometric collapse scores 0.149 and PASSES, while a
// stationary economy with ordinary ripple scores 1.009 and FAILS. The rule
// rewarded the disease and punished the cure, and it had done so since it was
// ported from notebooks/07_stability_suite.py.
//
// It is replaced by the two separate claims it was conflating:
//
//   DRIFTING  LogDrift(max_factor: 2.0)        the level must stay put
//   SWINGING  ResidualDamping(max_ratio: 2.0)  the wobble must not grow
//
// LogDrift is the OLS slope of ln(metric) against sample index, expressed as the
// total factor across the window and folded so a 3x fall and a 3x rise both
// score 3.0. It is registered as a total *across the window* rather than a rate
// per tick: it is a claim about the span actually observed, so a longer run is
// held to a proportionally tighter per-tick standard.
//
// ResidualDamping removes that fitted log-trend first, so a series is judged on
// how it moves about its own path rather than on where the path went. Its
// threshold is deliberately ABOVE 1.0: a real economy in equilibrium fluctuates
// persistently, and a rule demanding decay fails every healthy world. v1's 0.72
// encoded the assumption that a settled economy stops moving.
//
// HOW THE THRESHOLDS WERE CHOSEN â€” this matters more than their values. Both
// were fixed from the separation between synthetic healthy and synthetic sick
// series in tests/test_09_detectors.rs, BEFORE any scenario was scored with
// them. Healthy cases reach at most 1.20x drift and 1.03 oscillation; sick ones
// start at 3.0x drift and 4.2 oscillation. 2.0 sits in both gaps with margin on
// each side. A threshold picked to make particular scenarios pass is not a
// threshold (R6), and the test is the record that these were not.
//
// UNCHANGED FROM v1: the window (ticks 150..1000), every other class, every
// other threshold, and the fail-closed NaN policy. Only the detector changed, so
// a re-scored verdict differs only because the instrument was corrected.
//
// CHANGING A THRESHOLD AFTER SEEING RESULTS REQUIRES A NEW DATED FILE.
(
    version: 3,
    date: "2026-07-31",
    transient: 150,
    analysis_end: 1000,
    staple_good: "flour",
    labour_good: "labour",
    nan_policy: FailClosed,
    classes: [
        // A region with no transaction velocity is not an economy. Checked first
        // and short-circuits: once dead, nothing else about it is meaningful.
        (
            name: "DEAD",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.003, frac: 0.80),
            window: Analysis,
            short_circuit: true,
        ),
        (
            name: "DEAD_EMPLOYMENT",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Employment],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.05, frac: 0.80),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        // Short-term oscillation: the rolling coefficient of variation.
        (
            name: "UNSTABLE",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity, Employment, RealWage],
            rule: RollingCv(window: 10, max_cv: 0.12),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        // The level must stay put. Split out of v1's SWINGING, which read the
        // raw level and so scored any shrinking series as "settling" (see the
        // header). A metric that moves more than 2x across the window has gone
        // somewhere and not come back, whichever direction it went.
        (
            name: "DRIFTING",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity, RealWage],
            rule: LogDrift(max_factor: 2.0),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        // The wobble must not grow — measured on the detrended residual, so this
        // asks only about oscillation and not about where the level went.
        (
            name: "SWINGING",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Velocity, RealWage],
            rule: ResidualDamping(max_ratio: 2.0),
            window: Halves,
        ),
        // Currency pooling in buildings and still trending that way.
        (
            name: "CURRENCY_DRAIN",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [Concentration],
            rule: MeanAndSlope(mean_min: 0.82, slope_min: 0.0),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        (
            name: "POP_DESTITUTION",
            fatal: true,
            metrics: [RealIncome],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.8, frac: 0.50),
            window: Analysis,
        ),
        // Warning only: an idle plant is a symptom, not a failed region.
        (
            name: "DEAD_BUILDING",
            fatal: false,
            metrics: [BldUtil],
            rule: FracBelow(thresh: 0.05, frac: 0.60),
            window: PostTransient,
        ),
    ],
)
